Job Description:
Job Responsibilities
Develop media coverage strategies, coordinate media resources, and ensure accurate and timely information dissemination.
Draft press releases, official statements, and public opinion guidance materials to protect the company's legitimate rights and interests.
Contact media outlets (newspapers, television, online platforms), arrange interviews, filming, and reporting activities.
Monitor media coverage and social media public opinion in real time, analyze potential public relations risks, and provide response recommendations.
Participate in incident investigations and evidence collection, assist in preparing external promotional materials.
Regularly report on communication effectiveness and optimize follow-up media strategies.
Job Requirements
Education Requirement: Bachelor's Degree or above; candidates with majors in Journalism, Communication, Public Relations, or Law will be given priority。
Work Experience:‌ Minimum of 3 years’experience in media public relations, journalism, or industry publicity; familiar with media operations, skilled in press release writing, media relationship management, and crisis public relations; capable of independently completing reporting planning
No record of disciplinary violations, no complaints from industry associations, and no history of unethical or unprofessional conduct such as overcharging clients, failure to fulfill commitments, deception, threats, or harm to client interests (this is critical);
Possess strong professional ethics and dedication, be loyal to and protect client interests, be honest and trustworthy, reliable, committed to fulfilling promises, familiar with business etiquette, and mindful of personal branding;
Have solid professional competence and excellent job skills, capable of efficient collaboration with media, government agencies, and internal departments;
Possess strong logical analysis ability, negotiation skills, and interpersonal communication capabilities;
Experience in media public relations within the mining industry, familiar with procedures for handling illegal mining incidents;
Have media resources or industry connections, able to quickly reach target media;
Prior experience in international companies is preferred; standard English accent required;
Strong basic qualities, courteous demeanor, positive mindset, and appropriate, dignified behavior;
Fast learner, willing to continuously improve, ambitious, responsible, and self-motivated;
Capable of independently initiating and carrying out work, possess an innovative spirit, and able to complete the full cycle of planning, execution, and reporting;
Possess strong team spirit, organizational, coordination, communication, and leadership abilities; able to listen effectively and demonstrate outstanding interpersonal and social skills.
Compensation
Generous.

Core Responsibilities:
Advising and negotiating contracts and agreements with merchants, partners, and banks;
Liaising with regional Country Heads and Central Banks as required;
Embedding compliance with laws, regulations, business principles, and established best practices across governance, strategy, people, processes, policies, and culture;
Establishing and maintaining effective compliance risk management and control systems;
Providing timely advice on changes in compliance, privacy, and regulatory environments;
Supporting preparation and execution of fit-for-purpose contracts and legal documentation
Key Responsibilities & Activities:
Provide legal advice on commercial terms, technology and licensing, IP, data protection, marketing and advertising, and labor law;
Draft and negotiate legal documents including:
Service agreements
Vendor agreements
Sale agreements
Lease agreements
Confidentiality agreements
MOUs
Letters and third-party communications
Company secretarial services
Anticipate legal developments relevant to the business and advise on impact;
Support and oversee compliance across African jurisdictions in alignment with Chief Compliance and regional officers;
Assess compliance risks for new business models;
Advise and train management on legal and compliance risks;
Maintain and update regional compliance policies;
Foster strong legal, data protection, and compliance culture
Requirements:
Admitted Nigerian attorney with 2–3 years PQE;
Articles completed at a recognized corporate/commercial law firm;
At least 1 year in-house legal/compliance experience in fintech, payments, or financial services (preferred);
Strong stakeholder management and persuasion skills;
Act as DPO in Nigeria aligned with Group privacy governance;
Excellent English communication skills (written and verbal);
Risk management experience (strong plus);
Experience advising on payments/financial services regulatory matters (preferred);
Familiarity with card scheme rules (preferred);
Team player with cross-jurisdictional collaboration skills;
Ability to work independently and in a multinational, multicultural environment

Job Description
According to the company's overall strategy and development goals, actively develop and maintain good relations with various government departments (including standards bureau, immigration bureau, police station, court, customs, electricity) and banks and financial institutions, establish and maintain business contacts with various resources in the industry;
Collect and sort out the latest developments of local government policies, regulations or information, analyze and interpret the policies, plans and trends of the company's business development, propose coping strategies and rationalization suggestions, and strive for favorable resources for the company;
Effectively respond to and solve public relations crises and problems in the company's external activities;
Complete other tasks assigned by superiors.
Qualifications
Bachelor's Degree or above in Secretary, Business Administration, Marketing, Public Relations, International Business is preferred;
In-depth understanding and keen insight into industry trends, market dynamics and related policies;
Have rich working experience in public relations, public relations or related fields,
Be familiar with the working procedures of relevant government departments
Be able to handle various external affairs independently, and have the ability to solve complex problems;
High business sensitivity, good business thinking,
Able to grasp the market dynamics and customer needs, to provide targeted outreach strategies and suggestions for the company or project;
Language skills: Excellent oral and written English skills, able to convey information clearly and accurately;
Good at communication, excellent negotiation skills and coordination skills, and able to properly handle various complex interpersonal relationships.
Have strong coordination ability planning and execution ability, analysis and decision-making ability;
Comprehensive knowledge, excellent comprehensive quality, generous conversation, good personal image and manners, with a high degree of professional ethics and integrity awareness, able to keep business secrets, safeguard the interests of the company and customers.
Good team spirit, able to work closely with team members, with strong ability to work under pressure.
